      "why": "Fully pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax. To hit 32 Msps it needs Fmax >= 32 MHz, which is easy in sky130hd. The binding constraints are accuracy (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) and the 0.5 us p99 batch latency: a burst of 32 back-to-back requests through a fully pipelined unit takes 32 cycles + (N+2) latency. At >=32 MHz that is ~1 us + latency, so the batch bound is tight and will push toward lower N and higher Fmax. Area is minimised by the smallest data_width/n_iter that still clears 2^-12, so I focus the search on the low end of the accuracy/area trade-off (W 14-18, N 12-18) with modest guards and both rounding modes to find the cheapest point that meets error and the batch bound."
